Package: myna-desktop
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         ibus,
         pipewire,
Recommends: gnome-shell (>= 46),
            myna-config,
            myna-server-parakeet,
Description: offline push-to-talk dictation for the GNOME desktop
 Myna types what you say into the focused application. Press a shortcut,
 speak, press it again, and the transcript is injected through IBus.
 Audio stays on the machine: transcription runs in a local backend such as
 myna-server-parakeet.
 .
 This package holds the dictation daemon (a systemd user service), the HUD
 renderer and its GNOME Shell extension, and the settings schema.
 .
 Unofficial build of Myna by Canonical Ltd. (github.com/canonical/myna),
 with small patches, made by the macaw project. Not affiliated with or
 endorsed by Canonical.

Package: myna-server-parakeet
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         python3.13,
Recommends: myna-desktop,
Description: local speech recognition backend for Myna (Parakeet, CPU)
 Runs NVIDIA's Parakeet TDT 0.6B v3 model (25 languages, punctuation) as
 int8 ONNX on the CPU and serves it to myna-desktop over a Unix socket.
 .
 The model (about 800 MB) is not in this package. It downloads on the
 service's first start into ~/.cache/myna/models from a pinned URL and is
 checked against a SHA-256 hash. It is licensed CC-BY-4.0; credits are in
 /usr/share/doc/myna-server-parakeet/MODEL-NOTICE.
 .
 Unofficial build of Myna by Canonical Ltd. (github.com/canonical/myna),
 with small patches, made by the macaw project. Not affiliated with or
 endorsed by Canonical.

Package: myna-config
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         myna-desktop (= ${binary:Version}),
Description: settings for Myna dictation
 Myna Settings edits what the dictation daemon reads live: the keyboard
 shortcut, when to transcribe, the indicator, sounds, and the vocabulary of
 names and terms the model is biased toward. It also shows the installed
 model and a diagnostics report.
 .
 This build detects a package-based install and leaves models to the
 package manager: it installs, switches and configures nothing through snapd.
 .
 Unofficial build of Myna by Canonical Ltd. (github.com/canonical/myna),
 with small patches, made by the macaw project. Not affiliated with or
 endorsed by Canonical.
